    <statement><p>Let <m>V</m> be a vector space, <m>v, u \in V</m>, and let <m>T_1: V \rightarrow V</m> and <m>T_2: V \rightarrow V</m> be
linear transformations such that 
<me>T_1(v) = 5 v  - 5 u, \ \ \ T_1(u) = -7 v  - 2 u,</me>
<me>T_2(v) = 3 v + 2 u, \ \ \ T_2(u) = -7 v  - 5 u.</me>  
Find the images of <m>v</m> and <m>u</m> under the composite of <m>T_1</m> and <m>T_2</m>.</p>
<p><m>(T_2 T_1)(v) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,</p>
<p><m>(T_2 T_1)(u) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>50v+35u</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-7v+-4u</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
